From: RG35XX Java Platform
Task: RGJ-RC1-011BY
Subject: [PATCH] MobilePlatform: skip eager media engine on RG35XX

Historical hardware traces from the previously stable RG35XX platform show
runJar() skipped Manager.prepareMediaEngine() before loader.start(). The eager
upstream call initializes JavaSound/ALSA and touches /dev/snd/seq, which is not
present on the target and can prevent the MIDlet from reaching startApp().

Preserve upstream eager preparation for desktop/non-RG35XX runs. Explicit
RG35XX launches use the already-integrated lazy native MIDI/WAV bridge instead.

--- a/src/org/recompile/mobile/MobilePlatform.java
+++ b/src/org/recompile/mobile/MobilePlatform.java
@@ -819,7 +819,12 @@
 			 * Load up everything needed to play sound before the jar opens to minimize ingame stutters
 			 * this basically just loads up the synthesizers, as they're the biggest troublemakers.
 			 */
-			javax.microedition.media.Manager.prepareMediaEngine();
+			if(!RG35XXPlatformProfile.isActive())
+			{
+				javax.microedition.media.Manager.prepareMediaEngine();
+			}
+			else { Mobile.log(Mobile.LOG_INFO, "RG35XX: SKIPPING prepareMediaEngine; native media is lazy-initialized"); }
 
 			loader.start();
 		}
